Feature: slice-6 / empty-loading-error-states
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-6
Verified: 2026-05-28

What was built
==============
Animated skeleton placeholders replace the plain "Loading…" text
that used to fill the admin lists. Three concrete improvements:

1. TableSkeleton component
   - Renders 6 rows × N columns inside the same card+border chrome
     that the live tables use. Layout doesn't jump when data
     arrives.
   - Each cell renders a SkeletonBar with column-aware width:
     wider in column 0 (name/label), narrower in trailing columns
     (action / status / numeric).
   - Tailwind `animate-pulse` honours `prefers-reduced-motion`
     automatically, so the pulse stops for users who opted out.

2. CardSkeleton component
   - For OrgDetail's three-column card layout. Same border + bg
     pattern as the live `<Card>` so the swap is visually quiet.

3. Accessibility
   - The visible skeleton is `aria-hidden="true"`. A sr-only
     `<span role="status" aria-live="polite">` next to it carries
     the localized "loading…" text so screen readers still know
     what's happening.

Wired into:
- OrgsList.tsx        — 6-column TableSkeleton
- UsersList.tsx       — 5-column TableSkeleton
- AuditLogList.tsx    — 5-column TableSkeleton
- OrgDetail.tsx       — three CardSkeletons (Details / Therapists /
                        Recent activity) mirroring the live layout

Existing UX kept as-is
======================
The error + empty states across all four lists were already in good
shape (magma-bordered card with retry button for errors; serif text
for empty). They continue to use the existing translation keys; no
copy changes here.

Toast system: NOT added. The admin surfaces today only need inline
errors (returned from the action dialogs via ActionResult) and the
list-level retry banner. A toast would be over-engineering for the
current scope — flagged in PROGRESS.md as something to add if/when
the marketing pages get more interactive flows.

